futurama is undoubtedly one of the  greatest sci-fi comedies of all time but  despite its surprisingly tight and  well-thought-out timeline the series  didn't answer every question it raised  for example what became of bender's son  ben what happens to fry and leela after  the time bending events of the finale is  fry's old girlfriend michelle still  going out with the reanimated body of  paulie shore tis better to have loved  and lost nespa  the answers to all of these questions  could make for intriguing episodes ones  we'll likely never get to see and while  we can all live with a little mystery in  the year 3000 there's one lingering  question in particular that stands out  as particularly irksome what is the  other and why is she so important to the  universe's future we know who the other  is of course it's leela that's revealed  in the season 4 episode the wire fry  which is arguably one of the most  important futurama episodes ever made in  it fry learns that the accident that  landed him in the cryogenic freezing  tube and sent him to the future wasn't  actually an accident at all it was part  of a scheme by nibbler who spells  futurama's big secret during the episode  fry isn't just a doofus he's actually  the most important person in the entire  universe see because fry is his own  grandfather the former pizza delivery  boy is immune to attacks by the evil  brain spawn making him the only person  who can stop their plans for galactic  genocide in the wire fry the nibilonians  give fry a quantum interphase bomb and  send him off to fight the brain spawn  where he defeats them and saves the  entire galaxy  here we are trapped for eternity we  could sing american pie unfortunately  there's a complication as tends to be  the case with anything involving the  planet express crew and fry ends up back  in 1999 before he was frozen and sent to  the future after some time travel  shenanigans fry goes back to that  fateful moment when he became stuck in  the cryogenic unit it may seem like a  retcon but if you go back to watch the  futurama pilot you'll see nibbler's  shadow underneath where fry sat showing  how the creative team behind the sitcom  had their plan in place all along back  to season four and fry tries to stop  nibbler from sending his original body  to the year 3000. nibbler protests  however arguing that there must be  something in the future that fry thinks  is worth saving that's where the crucial  piece of dialogue comes in she must be  the other  what  [Music]  you must not give up on her fry doesn't  know what that means and we don't either  sadly it seems like we never will fox  canceled futurama after its fourth  season and while it came back from the  dead two times the writers never  bothered to explain what nibbler was  talking about given the why of fry's  important place in futurama canon  nibbler's words seem like they carry a  lot of weight or they would if they were  ever elaborated on of course in the  absence of a real explanation fans have  concocted their own theories many assume  that the nibilonians have plans for  leela that never made it to the screen  meanwhile some think that nibbler simply  meant that leela is the second most  important person in the universe as that  theory goes leela essentially saved the  galaxy by making fry care ultimately fry  decides to send his past self to the  future in the wire fry because he loves  leela as such she's indirectly  responsible for all of fry's heroics fry  is the one in the middle of things but  leela is the person who gives fry  something to fight for other fans  suggest that nibbler might be referring  to the series finale in which fry and  leela live together as a couple for  decades while everyone else around them  is stuck in time maybe it's even a star  wars reference nibbler and yoda have  some similarities after all although you  gotta hope that fry and leela aren't  secretly brother and sister whatever the  case fan theories are the only  explanations as to the other  significance that we're going to get by  all indications futurama isn't ever  coming back making this one big question  that's bound to go unanswered  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite shows are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one
 

